# The build context for every container image whose `image_build_context` is the repository root
# (search, libreoffice, discovery, ocr, recovery, file-repair — see each Worker's wrangler.jsonc).
#
# THIS FILE WAS REFERENCED BEFORE IT EXISTED. `containers/search/Dockerfile` has always said "The
# root .dockerignore keeps every crate's target/ out of the context", and there was no such file, so
# every root-context build shipped the whole repository to the daemon: node_modules, every crate's
# target/, the SPA build output, and .git. That is minutes of transfer per build for bytes no image
# has ever copied.
#
# ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST, and deliberately. Every one of those Dockerfiles copies exactly two
# things — `crates` and its own `containers/<name>` — so naming what may enter is both smaller and
# safer than trying to enumerate what may not: a new build artifact somewhere in the tree cannot
# quietly rejoin the context, because nothing rejoins it without a line here.
#
# This file does NOT affect scan, bundle or raster. Their images are built with their own directory
# as the context, and Docker reads the .dockerignore beside the context — not this one.
*

!crates
!containers

# Rust build output inside the two allowed trees. Re-excluded after the un-ignore above, because
# `!crates` would otherwise pull in gigabytes of `target/` from a developer's working tree — which is
# the exact cost the comment in containers/search/Dockerfile promised this file was preventing.
crates/**/target
containers/**/target
